libhybris: strip UBWC-triggering usage bits in HWComposerNativeWindow on sol

This is meta-aurora's libhybris-aurora-disable-ubwc-usage.patch, by Florent,
reused for sol. sol (Pixel Watch 3) is the same Qualcomm Monaco / sw5100 SoC as
aurora (Pixel Watch 2) and hits the identical display-pipeline limitation, so
the fix is the same. The diff is identical to aurora's apart from one comment
line naming the device, and it applies to the libhybris SRCREV this layer pins
with zero fuzz and zero offset.

QTI gralloc's IsUBwcEnabled() (hardware/qcom/<soc>/display/gralloc/gr_utils.cpp)
returns true when any of the following bits are set in the buffer usage:

  - GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER       = 0x800        (= BufferUsage::COMPOSER_CLIENT_TARGET)
  - GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_ALLOC_UBWC    = 0x10000000   (private bit 28; libEGL_adreno
                                                       adds this when creating an EGLSurface)
  - GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_ALLOC_UBWC_PI = 0x40000000   (private bit 30, "paddingless intra")

When IsUBwcEnabled returns true the allocator stamps the buffer with
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED at AddFB2 time. The only SDE SSPP available to
SDM for the launcher's client-composition layer is plane 70, a DMA pipe with no
UBWC support, so the atomic commit is rejected by the kernel.

Confirmed on sol hardware 2026-08-13, from the composer's own logs:

    E SDM: DRMAtomicReq::Commit: drmModeAtomicCommit failed with error 22
           (Invalid argument).
    E SDM: HWDeviceDRM::AtomicCommit: AtomicCommit failed with error -22 crtc 80
    E SDM: HWCDisplay::CommitLayerStack: Commit failed. Error = 11
    I SDM: HWDeviceDRM::DumpHWLayers: src_width = 512, src_height = 464,
           src_format = 12
    I SDM: HWDeviceDRM::DumpHWLayers: pipe = left_pipe, pipe_id = 70, z_order = 0

matching aurora's own reported symptom (`validate failed for display 0: 2`) --
sol's hwc2 compat layer reports the same error 2 out of validate. Everything
upstream of the commit is healthy on sol: the composer client is acquired, the
primary display hotplugs, Qt gets the real 456x456 panel, and validate/present
run in a continuous loop. Only the kernel-side commit fails, which is why the
connector stays "disabled" and crtc-0 stays enable=0/active=0.

HW_FB (0x1000) is NOT a UBWC trigger per gr_utils.cpp; EGL/libui need it for
the buffer to be a valid framebuffer surface. Keep it, add HW_RENDER and
HW_TEXTURE for GPU access, and strip the three UBWC triggers above.

Applied only on sol via SRC_URI:append:sol in the libhybris bbappend, so other
watches keep stock behavior bit-for-bit.

Note that this patch is NOT gated on HYBRIS_HWC_DISABLE_COMPOSER_USAGE, despite
what meta-aurora's bbappend comment says about its own copy: neither the aurora
original nor this one reads that variable anywhere. The gating is the
per-machine SRC_URI append, nothing else.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Florent Revest <revestflo@gmail.com>

--- a/egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp
+++ b/egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp
@@ -128,7 +128,12 @@
     m_width = width;
     m_height = height;
     m_bufFormat = format;
-    m_usage = GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER|GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB;
+    // sol (Pixel Watch 3 / Monaco): QTI gralloc's IsUBwcEnabled() returns
+    // true when usage has GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER. HW_FB is NOT a UBWC
+    // trigger; it's still needed so EGL/libui consider this a framebuffer
+    // surface. Strip HW_COMPOSER, add HW_RENDER|HW_TEXTURE for GPU access.
+    // Source: hardware/qcom/<soc>/display/gralloc/gr_utils.cpp.
+    m_usage = GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_RENDER|GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_TEXTURE|GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB;
     m_bufferCount = 2;
     m_nextBuffer = 0;
 }
@@ -434,7 +439,14 @@
  */
 int HWComposerNativeWindow::setUsage(uint64_t usage)
 {
-    usage |= GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER|GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB;
+    // Strip every flag QTI's IsUBwcEnabled() treats as a UBWC trigger:
+    //   - GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER         = 0x800       (= BufferUsage::COMPOSER_CLIENT_TARGET)
+    //   - GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_ALLOC_UBWC    = 0x10000000  (private bit 28; libEGL_adreno
+    //                                                       sets this on EGLSurface creation)
+    //   - GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_ALLOC_UBWC_PI = 0x40000000  (private bit 30, "paddingless intra")
+    // Source: hardware/qcom/<soc>/display/gralloc/gr_utils.cpp.
+    usage &= ~(uint64_t)(GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER | 0x10000000ULL | 0x40000000ULL);
+    usage |= GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_RENDER|GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_TEXTURE|GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB;
     int need_realloc = (m_usage != usage);
     TRACE("usage=x%" PRIx64 " realloc=%d", usage, need_realloc);
     m_usage = usage;
